From c3981f83837ac67c37ebd7a9f622481ddae9d805 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "MR. ARX" <dev@nexeris.dev>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 18:12:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix: signing out on one device was logging out every device

Root cause: components/TopNav.tsx's sign-out button called
supabase.auth.signOut() with no options. Supabase's default scope for
that call is 'global' -- it calls the server-side revoke endpoint and
invalidates the account's refresh token entirely, which kills every
active session for that account on every device/browser at once, not
just the one clicking "Sign out".

Fixed by passing { scope: 'local' }, which only clears this browser's
own session/storage without touching the server-side token -- so
signing out on phone no longer touches the desktop session, and vice
versa. Each device's session is now genuinely independent, the way a
normal sign-out button should behave.

Left the two signOut() calls in app/auth/callback/route.ts untouched
(still default/global scope) -- those aren't a user-initiated logout,
they're the security path that destroys a session the moment it's
discovered to belong to a disabled/unauthorized account right after
OAuth completes. That session was never legitimate, so revoking it
everywhere is the correct, intentional behavior there, not a bug.

Also verified (no code change needed): the auto-enable-restriction-
after-first-device logic from the previous patch is live and correct
as deployed. If it looked like it wasn't firing, that's very likely
because the tested account already had a device on record from before
that patch shipped -- it only triggers on an account's genuinely
first-ever device sighting, by design, not retroactively for existing
accounts/devices.
---
 components/TopNav.tsx | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/components/TopNav.tsx b/components/TopNav.tsx
index 8d8955c..eba409c 100644
--- a/components/TopNav.tsx
+++ b/components/TopNav.tsx
@@ -144,7 +144,15 @@ export function TopNav({
   async function handleLogout() {
     setLoggingOut(true);
     const supabase = createSupabaseBrowserClient();
-    await supabase.auth.signOut();
+    // scope: 'local' — clears only THIS browser's session. The default
+    // (no options / scope: 'global') calls Supabase's server-side revoke,
+    // which invalidates the account's refresh token everywhere at once —
+    // that's what was logging out every other device the moment any one
+    // of them signed out. Each device's session is meant to be
+    // independent; only an admin blocking/removing the account (or the
+    // "Log out all" enforce-devices action) should ever affect other
+    // devices, not a normal sign-out button.
+    await supabase.auth.signOut({ scope: 'local' });
     router.push('/login');
     router.refresh();
   }
